{"id":"q05","run":1,"role":"calibration","category":"puzzle","question":"A patch of lily pads triples in size every day and first covers the whole lake on day 30. Is exactly half the lake covered on day 29?","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":null,"claims":[{"text":"In the classic lily-pad puzzle the patch doubles daily.","confidence":0.95,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.4923,"phi":1.1627},{"text":"With doubling, the patch covers half the lake the day before full coverage.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.6469},{"text":"Someone relying on the doubling pattern might wrongly answer yes.","confidence":0.8,"lean":1,"theta":1.2566,"phi":1.7758},{"text":"This version of the puzzle has the patch tripling daily.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":2.8979},{"text":"With tripling and full coverage on day 30, day-29 coverage is one-third of the lake.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":2.8867},{"text":"Half coverage on day 29 would require a growth factor of 2, which is not given.","confidence":0.93,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4608,"phi":2.6907},{"text":"Nothing else in the question, like a change in lake size or different growth rule, would make half correct.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":2.7874},{"text":"The tripling rate plus full coverage on day 30 decides the question, so the answer is no.","confidence":0.96,"lean":-1,"theta":1.508,"phi":2.8308}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":4,"J":-0.4,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":-0.4,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":2,"j":4,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":5,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":6,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":7,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":4,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":5,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":6,"J":0.